{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/983975-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-errata-thread","id":983975,"title":"Kinfolk: A Breed Apart errata thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-08T10:46:55-07:00","id":983975,"title":"Kinfolk: A Breed Apart errata thread","content":"Please report typos and visual glitches in <i>Kinfolk: A Breed Apart</i> here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T11:23:14-07:00","id":983986,"title":"","content":"In case you didnt check the other thread allready reported there, that their seems to be a bug in the renown chart where you lose Wisdom for bearing Garou offspring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T13:17:35-07:00","id":984026,"title":"","content":"There are a few non-Errata things worth checking out in the other thread as well, Rose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7621-threadwrought","name":"Threadwrought","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T02:09:19-07:00","id":984319,"title":"","content":"For the sake of consolidation, I'll repeat this here. In the section on Numina, there's a reference to a 'following chart' that's supposed to list freebie point and experience point costs. The closest thing to said chart is about twenty pages earlier, on page 58. It only lists freebie point costs, implies that a given Kinfolk can only have two Numina, and there are asterisks with no footnotes or references attached.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T11:04:29-07:00","id":984498,"title":"","content":"Page 11, &quot;Being Kinfolk&quot; - straight comparisons to warfare are too clean, since the Garou are largely fighting an asymmetric war now.<br /> <br /> Page 16: Why would the Get go out of their way to pair with Germanic/Teutonic/North Europeans when said folk largely venerated their worst enemies in antiquity, and don't have the &quot;qualities&quot; listed that the Get are supposedly looking for in modern times (if you're looking for a warrior culture... there are very few of them, and Northern Europe largely doesn't practice one anymore, leaving folk like the Gurkhas in rarefied company)? And why would they care about having a father at the head of any given family rather than a werewolf? All of the Revised Tribebook's major strides are being tossed aside here.<br /> <br /> Page 17, sidebar on the lord's right: &quot;Though not a confirmed fact, enough references to the practice exist to presume that high-born men, particularly in a society that valued women only as commodities for vessels or breeding, did exercise this prerogative.&quot;<br /> <br /> [CITATION NEEDED], because I think I recall hearing a fair amount of evidence arguing the opposite case.<br /> <br /> Page 18, Fenrir and Shadow Lords preferring to admit primarily male Garou and being spear-side versions of the Black Furies: This is not how things have ever worked, and there was no hint in any prior material that it would or should be the future.<br /> <br /> Page 19: Children of Gaia expecting kin to perform in combat to the same degree as Garou. Why would they do that? There's no compelling reason to imagine why they or anyone else would.<br /> <br /> Page 20: I don't see a compelling reason for Get to have ever held men in higher esteem over women. It's something that doesn't matter when everyone turns into a death machine.<br /> <br /> Page 21: Reference to Gaia using the pronoun &quot;her&quot; not capitalized.<br /> <br /> Page 22: Again, there's no compelling reason that the Shadow Lords would be more male than female.<br /> <br /> Page 23: Last paragraph of Silver Fangs makes what seems to be a reference to Tribal Flaws, which are generally not a thing.<br /> <br /> I am not sure of how to parse the second paragraph's reference to &quot;mysticism of the east&quot;, Does it mean that the Stargazers preferred kin among religious sects, or something else?<br /> <br /> Page 26: Actually having sacrificed Turtle as well is a rather large change. Regarding the White Howlers, the Picts weren't Celts.<br /> <br /> Page 28: A battalion is typically several hundred people. If you only have a single hundred, then you more likely have a company.<br /> <br /> Schwartz is firmly against retiring in the beginning of the passage, but makes jokes about it at the end of it. Those ends could be smoothed down a bit.<br /> <br /> Page 29: Dating back 600 years would put you in the 15th rather than 16th century.<br /> <br /> Page 32: You meet an avatar of Gaia, or more likely, of her avatar's avatar. If you meet Gaia Herself (note the capitalization), you wouldn't be able to process it, particularly if not part spirit.<br /> <br /> Page 33: Catholic Fianna and Protestant Get is probably not the best tack to take, even if trying to present it as a mere trend. Get definitely wouldn't be revering the Aesir; the only reason they would have to hang around Norse pagans would be to beat them up and either break or desecrate their profane idols. Similarly, the Furies probably wouldn't venerate much of the Greek Pantheon; the only ones they don't hate are Artemis, Hecate, Hestia, Demeter, and Persephone. They typically venerate the Gorgons as well; this should be illustrative of how much they value traditional practice of worship to the Greco-Roman deities (i.e. not very much at all).<br /> <br /> Also, with the mention that Uktena and Wendigo follow tribal customs, you mean the Garou tribe, right?<br /> <br /> Page 35: right under the entry for Callow Kinfolk, there's a break in a line between the &quot;a&quot; and &quot;bout&quot; components of about.<br /> <br /> Page 37: Red Talons don't take on jobs. They don't have the documentation to do so, nor do they have any means to fake said documentation, since they all live out in the wilderness and eschew connections with human society. They stay out of human form as much as possible. I can see some more tolerant Red Talons eavesdropping on the people with those jobs and looking over the shoulders of wildlife biologists using concealment and invisibility Gifts in order to glean information, but not Red Talons with employment.<br /> <br /> Page 39: Category for rite of discovery missing.<br /> <br /> Page 45: Sentience goes hand in hand with being alive.<br /> <br /> Page 48: Simply put, the Mokole entry reflects information that we have on corrupted Mnetics and not any detail of actual Mokole. It genuinely requires a full replacement to put it inline with W20 Changing Breeds.<br /> <br /> Page 50: Again, as noted on the other thread, Rokea do not have shark kinfolk as such; any pairing with a shark produces one, or rarely more, newborn Rokea. Kinfolk refers entirely to kadugo. What this passage says on sharks is also generally ill-informed and vastly, overly broad.<br /> <br /> Page 51: Castle Bravo going off at Turna'a killed half of the Rokea alive at the time, not 75%. Rokea are also not inherently solitary, as they're one of the few breeds other than Garou to form a pack-like association.<br /> <br /> Regarding the Hengeyokai, the placement of contrasts that is &quot;eastern vs. western&quot; is much less of a concern for Garou and Fera. The influence of Confucianism is unlikely to really foul up Garou, who also venerate their ancestors, and have a set of relationships in their culture that defines much of how social interaction works.. &quot;Ritual and control&quot;? Also, really, really important to Garou. Remember that in spite of being called &quot;the Western Concordiat&quot;, the Garou Nation is very much not like a modern European culture. Also, members of the Beast Courts still have Rage, and are proponents of an inhuman and primordial order, just as with the the Garou and Fera.<br /> <br /> Page 52: &quot;More numerous than wolves are in Japan&quot; is far beyond damning with faint praise. It suggests that there are wolves IRL in Japan to compare populations, which is clearly not the case, secret Garou-guarded packs or not.<br /> <br /> Page 58: Intuition's mechanical aims as described already exist in the form of Empathy and Enigmas. I also don't see why Meditation is one of its specialties.<br /> <br /> Page 59: Bureaucracy has a rights protection specialty; would this not fall under Law instead?<br /> <br /> Herbalism has a lot of overlap with Science except for its mystic touches.<br /> <br /> There's no system established to differentiate the Medicine Ability from the Veterinary Medicine Ability, other than the latter is more limited. Also, the descriptions jump ahead as a result of the bizarre way of WW couching Knowledge titles by level.<br /> <br /> Page 77: Wolfsbane has always been a strictly optional weakness to Garou; its name comes from Greek and refers strictly to non-Garou wolves being killed.<br /> <br /> Page 78: Is there some kind of correspondence intended for all of those toxicity tables, with regard to an Equipment rating for poisons?<br /> <br /> Page 82: Why do the paths on this page have weird Ability requirements instead of Occult?<br /> <br /> Page 85: True Faith is reproduced from older versions of the game that still use the 1-10 scale, as opposed to the Hunter's Hunted 2 version that goes from 1-5.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 10-10-2016, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T11:08:59-07:00","id":984500,"title":"","content":"on page 20, the Get being (somewhat) misogynistic is a long running thing, get rid of that, you get rid of the valkyries of the Freyas reason to exist<br /> <br /> Page 85 I agree with you, the True faith of 6+ is ssomething that should be forgotten as an embarassment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T11:14:38-07:00","id":984509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/983975-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-errata-thread?p=984500#post984500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">on page 20, the Get being (somewhat) misogynistic is a long running thing, get rid of that, you get rid of the valkyries of the Freyas reason to exist</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that they're a camp named after one of the Aesir and not maiming said Aesir, they already don't have any compelling reason to exist. Any further arguments can be taken to another thread.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T12:21:43-07:00","id":984548,"title":"","content":"In agreement with Saur Ops on their points. -nods-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7621-threadwrought","name":"Threadwrought","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T12:42:09-07:00","id":984554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/983975-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-errata-thread?p=984498#post984498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Page 48: Simply put, the Mokole entry reflects information that we have on corrupted Mnetics and not any detail of actual Mokole. It genuinely requires a full replacement to put it inline with W20 Changing Breeds.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely going to agree that I hope this gets changed. I know that the errata thread is meant to be more about print glitches and what not, but altering this would mean a lot. It takes away one of my favorite aspects about the Mokole culture. Also I remember the segment on corrupted Mnesis was originally stemming from a part of the draft that rubbed a lot of the fans on the KS the wrong way, and was later changed to represent corrupted memories. I hope it gets changed for these reasons but also to keep a smoother narrative if it stays in line with the previous splat written on the topic (such as the idea of the 8th sun in the breed book). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T14:46:53-07:00","id":984605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/983975-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-errata-thread?p=984498#post984498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 17, sidebar on the lord's right: &quot;Though not a confirmed fact, enough references to the practice exist to presume that high-born men, particularly in a society that valued women only as commodities for vessels or breeding, did exercise this prerogative.&quot;<br /> <br /> [CITATION NEEDED], because I think I recall hearing a fair amount of evidence arguing the opposite case.<br /> <br /> Page 18, Fenrir and Shadow Lords preferring to admit primarily male Garou and being spear-side versions of the Black Furies: This is not how things have ever worked, and there was no hint in any prior material that it would or should be the future.<br /> <br /> Page 19: Children of Gaia expecting kin to perform in combat to the same degree as Garou. Why would they do that? There's no compelling reason to imagine why they or anyone else would.<br /> <br /> Page 20: I don't see a compelling reason for Get to have ever held men in higher esteem over women. It's something that doesn't matter when everyone turns into a death machine.<br /> <br /> Page 21: Reference to Gaia using the pronoun &quot;her&quot; not capitalized.<br /> <br /> Page 22: Again, there's no compelling reason that the Shadow Lords would be more male than female.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm siding with Prince of the Night on this one. That's how the Get have <i>always</i> been written. It doesn't have to make logical sense -- it just has to make sense to a bunch of testosterone-laden-jock-douches with superpowers (like pretty much every male Get). You get rid of it (presumably because you want the Garou to be appear so much more noble) you pretty drastically change what the Get of Fenris tribe is thematically.<br /> <br /> 17: Whether or not it's provable IRL, there's enough room to maneuver in World of Darkness to leave that to creative license. Moreover it really recaptures the true horror of existence as a Kinfolk: Namely that your <i>only</i> real purpose in life is as slave and sex-toy for the Garou -- and they're the <i>good</i> guys!<br /> <br /> 19: Because Kin get called upon to guard the caern since there's too few Garou to do the job anymore, also since it allows them to involve their Kin more (and reduce the Garou/Kin friction as much as possible -- since they're the CoG's that that's one of the cornerstones of the tribal philosophy).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T16:56:52-07:00","id":984654,"title":"","content":"The Get have always been written that way. If that's what they are, that's what they are.<br /> <br /> I see no problem with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T17:05:57-07:00","id":984657,"title":"","content":"Glad to see people agree with me. <br /> <br /> <br /> Lets continue this conversation here though shall we, for ease of the developers? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf\"> Kinfolk: A Breed Apart in PDF - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/982463-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-in-pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I'm surprised that no one has mentioned it before me, but Kinfolk: A Breed Apart (https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/194952?affiliate_id=498510) is now on sale. Discuss. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 10-09-2016, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T20:29:02-07:00","id":984732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/983975-kinfolk-a-breed-apart-errata-thread?p=984554#post984554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Definitely going to agree that I hope this gets changed. I know that the errata thread is meant to be more about print glitches and what not, but altering this would mean a lot. It takes away one of my favorite aspects about the Mokole culture. Also I remember the segment on corrupted Mnesis was originally stemming from a part of the draft that rubbed a lot of the fans on the KS the wrong way, and was later changed to represent corrupted memories. I hope it gets changed for these reasons but also to keep a smoother narrative if it stays in line with the previous splat written on the topic (such as the idea of the 8th sun in the breed book).</div> </div> </div> </div>I also agree with this. Mokole need all the help they can get surviving in modern times, why would they make it harder on themselves by mistreating their support structures?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member